<P>Congress granted to the Treasury Secretary the authority to prescribe regulations that would allow taxpayers the option of deducting, rather than capitalizing, intangible drilling and development costs.  The Secretary's rules state that, in general, the option to deduct IDC applies only to  expenditures for drilling and development items that do not have a salvage value.</P>
